Subject: base-files: replace /tmp/TZ atomically

OpenWrt's musl maps /etc/TZ, a link to /tmp/TZ, afresh on every
localtime call. The system service rewrites the file in place, so a
reload truncates it under any process converting a time at that moment,
and that process reads the emptied mapping and dies with SIGBUS. Write
the new zone to a temporary file and rename it over /tmp/TZ.

Start9 downstream patch (start-technologies projects/start-wrt).
Applies to: openwrt v25.12.6

--- a/package/base-files/files/etc/init.d/system
+++ b/package/base-files/files/etc/init.d/system
@@ -21,7 +21,8 @@
 
 	echo "$hostname" > /proc/sys/kernel/hostname
 	[ -z "$conloglevel" -a -z "$buffersize" ] || dmesg ${conloglevel:+-n $conloglevel} ${buffersize:+-s $buffersize}
-	echo "$timezone" > /tmp/TZ
+	echo "$timezone" > /tmp/TZ.$$
+	mv -f /tmp/TZ.$$ /tmp/TZ
 	[ -n "$zonename" ] && [ -f "/usr/share/zoneinfo/${zonename// /_}" ] \
 		&& ln -sf "/usr/share/zoneinfo/${zonename// /_}" /tmp/localtime \
 		&& rm -f /tmp/TZ
